Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||07-07-2001||11:34 PM||||My drivers side is starting to fail. The left motor spins after going up for about ten sec, and once or twice did not go all the way up.<P>I've searched back thru the old posts<P>I see Rodney Dickmans web site talked about having a 1987 - 1988 Headlight Kit<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87-88headlight.jpg"> <P>Kit contains 3 precision machined Delrin bushings and excellent rebuilding instructions. <P>Has anyone used this kit ?  What kind of job it it ? <P>Thank you for any info.||||reg||5
Z||000001||hyhy4u||07-08-2001||12:29 AM||||Ive never heard anything about that kit...but i just pulled the three bushings out of a late 80's Sunbird motors and now mine work great..its not to hard to replace them..you can kindof figure it out as you go along..||||reg||1
Z||000002||kempo||07-08-2001||12:52 AM||||Got this kit when I needed both lights to be rebuilt.  After rebuilding them, I laugh at everybody who goes to the junkyard to get light motors.  The directions are literally right on.  I installed it on my old '87 coupe when both actuators went on me.  For $8 you can get both rebuilt... DO IT!!  I highly recommend it!  You're only looking at about 2 hours total on rebuilding them (that's if you really are taking your time.)  I rebuilt both of mine within an hour.  Best of luck!<P>-Kemp||||reg||14
