Z||000008||mrfixit58||07-08-2001||12:23 PM||||CoolBlue,<P>Fixing the headlights on an 87-88 is one the easiest jobs there is. The trick is gaining access. I use a 10MM socket on a 6" extension and LOOSEN the bottom two nuts then REMOVE to top two nuts. Then, just unplug the headlight and motor connectors and the whole assembly -- frame and all -- comes out. Then just unbolt the pivot arm from the motor and the three bolts holding the motor to the frame. Remove and replace the old bushings and reverse the procedure to re-assemble.<P>When you remove the three 7MM bolts to pull the cover on the motors, be sure to note the thrust washers on each side of the drive gear and don't tear the gasket. Clean the housing of all old crud and use a small amount of new grease.<P>I did both headlights on my brother-in-law's 87 in 45 minutes. Your first will take longer but not much.<P>Good luck,<P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||12
